--- An argument no row of the name takes is refused beside an argument
--- whose kind is not known yet, which may be any: `window`'s third
--- argument is text, and `3` is an int whatever `f` turns out to be. Any
--- argument of no known kind had spared the whole call, and the lowering
--- handed the int to the text parameter — "internal error: the lowered
--- program disagrees with itself", in a function nothing calls
use frame

fn unused[f]
    return frame.window[f, 'qty', 3, 'sum']

log[1]
